  "reason": "The records collectively establish several relevant directions: molecular-dynamics deformation of compositionally similar FCC HEAs, lower dislocation density and strength at high temperature, increasing HCP fractions during deformation, temperature-dependent stacking-fault and dislocation processes, and thermal reductions in elastic stiffness. Nanoindentation and structure–hardness/modulus relationships are also known in other HEAs. However, none combines a FeNiCrCoCu coating on Cu with temperature-controlled nanoindentation and friction, nor predicts the specific stability through 600 K followed by disorder-driven softening and increased friction above 900 K. Selecting this coated geometry, indentation/friction protocol, and threshold mechanism would therefore require a substantial additional idea."
